messages "Walla**Subj: ideasDate: Dec 21This is pretty much a direct loan from another person on another mud, butI think it pretty well sums up what I intend to say If you truly wish for something to happen, like those weapons, try to refineyour idea somewhat further. Just going 'give us these' isn't very inspiring,and it doesnt answer to the most important question. The question being \"why?\".If you do not wish to answer the other important questions, please do take thetime to answer that particular one at least to raise intrest. What im getting at, is that although any idea with \"code this\", might be fine,most wizards can come up with such ideas all by themselves, so what makes youridea special and worth doing?. Heres a list of a few other things I'd personally like to know when someonesuggests an idea of a race/guild/skill/weapontype/whatever: 1) Why should it be done, whats special about it?2) Where does it fit in the scheme of things, if its an offensive skill, whatis its purpose in a mud with dozens of such skills already, besides somenew messages and generally being \"cool\"3) Who should get this skill/whatever, and why do just _they_ need somethingextra?4) Would it make some other thing(skill/etc) useless by existing, and if yes,is it all around a better system of things than the replaced one.5) How does it improve this mud? For the last question, suitable answers wouldnt be \"itd make guild x suckFor the last question, suitable answers wouldnt be \"itd make guild x suck;less\", or \"itd improve my rate\", or itd make thing Y and Z useful again.In my opinion, should you state such claims, itd have more weight if you saidwhy things Y and Z are useless as they are, and what the effect of the systemyou are proposing to them would be.  And finally, if you think this is all too much trouble to go through just tosuggest something, consider the trouble spent coding a suggestion like this.  -Walla**"
